{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Root cause and platform dependence (re-measured 2026-10-31, before claim)\n\nThe trap is **macOS-only**. Linux CI's git handles `\\b` in `-E` correctly, so AC3 as written (\"asserts the documented divergence\") would fail on the gating `ubuntu-latest` cell.\n\nFixture: `alpha beta` / `alphabeta`, pattern `alpha\\b`.\n\n| Host / git | `-E` | `-G` (BRE) | `-P` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| macOS, Homebrew git 2.56.0 | line 2 `alphabeta` (wrong) | line 1 | line 1 |\n| macOS, Apple Git 2.54.0 (Apple Git-157) | line 2 `alphabeta` (wrong) | line 1 | line 1 |\n| Debian 12 (glibc 2.36) container, git 2.39.2 | line 1 (correct) | line 1 | line 1 |\n\nPortable forms gave line 1 on every host: `-E '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])alpha([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)'`, `-w`, `-P`. Note `-E '\\<alpha\\>'` matched nothing on macOS (rc 1), so `\\<`/`\\>` is not a portable substitute either.\n\n**Mechanism (git source, v2.56.0):** since git 2.38 (1819ad327b, \"grep: fix multibyte regex handling under macOS\") macOS git compiles patterns with the native libc regex instead of `compat/regex/`. `compat/regcomp_enhanced.c` (added 54463d32ef67, git 2.40) adds `REG_ENHANCED` — the macOS flag that enables `\\b`, `\\w`, `\\<` — **only when `REG_EXTENDED` is unset**: `if (!(cflags & REG_EXTENDED)) cflags |= REG_ENHANCED;`. So BRE (`-G`, the default) gets `\\b`; ERE (`-E`) does not, and macOS ERE reads `\\b` as a literal `b`. On Linux, glibc `regcomp` supports `\\b` as a GNU extension in both BRE and ERE.\n\nAlso: the ticket's \"system `grep -nE`\" row is unaffected on macOS too (`/usr/bin/grep` BSD grep 2.6.0 gave line 1).\n\nCI coverage note: macOS CI runs only `platform_compat`-marked tests (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:755`), applied by path via `_PLATFORM_COMPAT_PATH_FRAGMENTS` in `tests/conftest.py`. A test that pins the macOS divergence runs in macOS CI only if its path is listed there."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793487485717610001,"uuid":"bbb152bc-0191-4f3d-9e04-127651aa4dbb"}